From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 22:15:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] arm: rtd129x: drop the MMU state that the vendor U-Boot
 leaves

The vendor U-Boot "go" starts this U-Boot with the MMU on. Then
dcache_enable() keeps the vendor page tables. U-Boot relocates over
them, and a later load to 0x20200000 gets a translation fault.

Turn the MMU off in arch_cpu_init() when it is on. U-Boot then sets
up its own page tables.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 arch/arm/Kconfig            |  1 +
 arch/arm/mach-rtd129x/soc.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/Kconfig b/arch/arm/Kconfig
index f557f9dd0c..add69616ec 100644
--- a/arch/arm/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/Kconfig
@@ -1098,6 +1098,7 @@ config ARCH_OWL
 
 config ARCH_RTD129X
 	bool "Realtek RTD1295/RTD1296 SoCs"
+	select ARCH_CPU_INIT
 	select ARM64
 	select GICV2
 	select OF_SYSTEM_SETUP
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rtd129x/soc.c b/arch/arm/mach-rtd129x/soc.c
index 14529f0ba8..a0f822b5a9 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rtd129x/soc.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rtd129x/soc.c
@@ -50,6 +50,19 @@ static struct mm_region rtd129x_mem_map[] = {
 
 struct mm_region *mem_map = rtd129x_mem_map;
 
+/*
+ * The vendor U-Boot's "go" leaves its MMU on. dcache_enable() then keeps
+ * the vendor's page tables, which lie where this U-Boot relocates to.
+ * Start without them.
+ */
+int arch_cpu_init(void)
+{
+	if (get_sctlr() & CR_M)
+		dcache_disable();
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 int dram_init(void)
 {
 	return fdtdec_setup_mem_size_base();
